  "line": "Egypt is the land of the Nile, where Joseph rose to power, Jacob's family grew into a nation, and God later brought Israel out.",
  "moments": [
    {
      "title": "Joseph Sold to Potiphar",
      "text": "Joseph's brothers sold him to traders who took him to Egypt. There the Midianites sold him to Potiphar, an officer of Pharaoh.",
      "passage": "Genesis 37:25-36"
    },
    {
      "title": "Joseph Placed Over Egypt",
      "text": "Pharaoh put Joseph in charge of all the land of Egypt. Joseph then stored up food in the cities during the seven years of plenty.",
      "passage": "Genesis 41:41-48"
    },
    {
      "title": "Jacob's Family Goes to Egypt",
      "text": "God told Jacob not to be afraid to go down to Egypt, and promised to make his family a great nation there. Jacob and all his descendants then went to Egypt.",
      "passage": "Genesis 46:1-8"
    },
    {
      "title": "The Midwives Fear God",
      "text": "A new king who did not know Joseph came to power. He ordered the Hebrew midwives to kill baby boys, but they feared God and let the boys live.",
      "passage": "Exodus 1:8-19"
    },
    {
      "title": "The Exodus",
      "text": "At midnight the LORD struck down every firstborn male in the land of Egypt, from Pharaoh's firstborn to the prisoner's, and the firstborn of the livestock too. The Egyptians urged the Israelites to leave, and after 430 years the LORD's divisions went out of Egypt.",
      "passage": "Exodus 12:29-42"
    }
  ],
  "sources": [
    "BSB"
  ]
